    "narrative": "With a light schedule today, the Austin Waves offense faces a challenging test against Nola, A, who continues to command a formidable 3.87 xERA. **Jorge Polanco** holds a marginal score of 53.39, buoyed slightly by favorable wind conditions providing a 5% boost to his power potential. While his platoon disadvantage against a right-hander and Nola's command temper expectations, **Jorge Polanco** remains our primary offensive focal point given the limited availability of our core stars. We are effectively in a preservation phase, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are all inactive, forcing us to lean on depth pieces like **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** to anchor the production floor. The lack of elite speed options in tonight\u2019s lineup is glaring; with **Luis Robert Jr.** still sidelined on the IL, we are navigating a period where stolen base accumulation will be stagnant, forcing us to prioritize lineup efficiency over high-ceiling aggression.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision centered on the utility slot, where **Nasim Nunez** just narrowly missed the cut behind our current configuration. While the speed upside of **Nasim Nunez** is exactly the profile we prioritize to climb the 5x5 standings, his current batting order position and a projected lack of plate appearances capped his efficiency score below the 40-point \"start\" threshold. We are monitoring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** closely for any late-breaking lineup shifts; should the weather outlook in their respective parks deteriorate further, we will pivot to **Jacob Wilson** or **Heliot Ramos** to ensure we don't bleed points on empty at-bats. Beyond the starters, the organization continues to track the development of **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Josh Jung**, though none currently grade out as viable starters for today\u2019s rotation. Owners should note that **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Denzer Guzman**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Cole Carrigg** remain on the roster periphery, held in reserve to maximize our daily game caps for the remainder of the week.",
